; Tutorial_3_Open_a_Database_and_Move_Through_Records.inix -- opening a database and finding your way.

[about]
Title=3 - Open a Database and Move Through Records
Intro=A template database opened from the Help menu, and moving through it by row, by column, by search and by record number.
Setup=DbDo is installed.
Homework=Open another template database and find a record by keyword.

[step]

Say=One want: a database open and a record found in it, quickly. DbDo ships template databases to practice on; JobTrail tracks job applications.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus D, D for DbDo, opens it or brings it forward.
Key=Alt+Control+D
Hear=DbDo
Hear=DbDo ready

[step]

Say=Control plus O, O for Open, opens a database file. The templates are in the Help menu, under Template Databases; I open JobTrail.
Key=Control+O
Hear=Open Database dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I choose JobTrail and press Enter. Shift plus Z says where I am.
Key=Shift+Z
Hear=jobs, 12 records, no filter, sorted by employer

[step]

Say=Down Arrow moves by record; Right Arrow by column. Control plus G, G for Go, goes to a record by its number.
Key=Control+G
Hear=Go to Record dialog
Hear=Record number: edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type 7 and press Enter.
Key=Enter
Hear=(record 7, its first column first)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus K, K for Keywords, searches every column for words.
Key=Control+K
Hear=Keywords dialog
Hear=Keywords: edit
Hear=Type in text.
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type Seattle and press Enter.
Key=Enter
Hear=(the first record holding Seattle)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=F3 goes to the next match, Shift plus F3 to the one before. Alt plus Delete says the column and the row number.
Key=Alt+Delete
Hear=(the column's name, row 3)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A planned misstep: Control plus F is not find here. In DbDo, F is for Filter, a later walk. Keywords is K. Escape leaves anything opened by mistake.
Key=Escape
Hear=DbDo
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Keywords searches every column; Jump searches one. Control plus J, Jump to Record, asks which column and what to look for.
Key=Control+J
Hear=Jump to Record dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I choose employer, type Amazon, and press Enter. The cursor lands on the first job there.
Key=Enter
Hear=Amazon, employer, row 5
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Shift plus J jumps backward to the one before, and Control plus Shift plus K does the same for Keywords: Shift reverses, here as everywhere in DbDo.
Key=Control+Shift+J
Hear=Amazon, employer, row 2
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus Y, Say Yield, says how many records there are.
Key=Shift+Y
Hear=12 records
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus C, Say Cell, says the value under the cursor again, without moving.
Key=Shift+C
Hear=Amazon
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus L, Say Column as List, reads every value in the column, top to bottom, a quick way to hear what a column holds.
Key=Alt+L
Hear=Amazon, Boeing, Costco, Microsoft
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus I, Inspect Record, shows the whole record at once, one field to a line.
Key=Control+I
Hear=Inspect Record dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape. A database can hold several tables; Control plus T, Choose Table, lists them.
Key=Control+T
Hear=Choose Table dialog, jobs, 1 of 3
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape keeps the table I am in.
Key=Escape
Hear=jobs, 12 records
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the command; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Open a database.
Key=
Hear=Control plus O

[step]

Say=Go to a record by number.
Key=
Hear=Control plus G

[step]

Say=Search every column.
Key=
Hear=Control plus K
